        <briefdescription>
<para>Issue a fencing command against <computeroutput>node_id</computeroutput>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The implementation should ensure the target node can no longer write to the cluster before returning. If it cannot guarantee this within the given <computeroutput>deadline</computeroutput>, it should return false.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>node_id</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Node to fence. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>reason</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Human-readable reason (for audit log). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>deadline</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Latest point at which fencing must be confirmed. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>true if the node was successfully fenced, false otherwise. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
